{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1487850-need-some-ideas-for-nautical-themed-tempest-adventure","id":1487850,"title":"Need some ideas for nautical themed Tempest adventure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-25T01:56:01-07:00","id":1487850,"title":"Need some ideas for nautical themed Tempest adventure","content":"Ahoy! I'm planning a nautical scenario that's going to be a Wraith reskin of <i>Moby Dick + Rime of the Ancient Mariner</i> and then segues into <i>20,000 Leagues Under the Tempest + Das Boot</i>. Ahab/Nemo is going to be a Ferryman NPC who hunts part of his Psyche that got separated and lost in the Tempest. Players are going to be crew of the relic vessel- a WW2 era submarine probably. I have <i>Sea of Shadows</i> and there's a lot of useful material in there for the first part, but I'm struggling with a few specifics, especially for the second part. It's been decades since I last ran a Wraith game, and I think I'm a bit rusty.<br /> <br /> First of, Argos. I'm very sure at least one player is going to pick some dots in Argos, and I'm a bit concerned that it might trivialize some of the story elements. I need a good explanation to limit the reach of some abilities without shutting it down unfairly. Navigating the Tempest in proximity around the vessel is fine, I just don't want them to peace out to the next Necropolis.<br /> <br /> Next, recovery. I have no experience how well regaining Pathos/Corpus works while in a bottled environment like a submarine for a long time. Running out of 'food' is a classic for nautical adventures, but I don't want the players to starve either. Any advice on this is very welcome.<br /> <br /> For the second part, I had the idea that truly ancient lost cities sunk into the depths of the Tempest, and have the players explore them. If possible I would like to avoid places that players might know from other splats because they have relevance there, like Carthage or Enoch. I have some ideas for G\u00f6bekli Tepe and Harappa, but more ideas and what encounters they hold are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T05:36:49-07:00","id":1487875,"title":"","content":"Going by the powers listed in Wr20, I don't think you have much to worry about until the Argos 5 Initiate power. Most of the powers are effectively personal. Stormreader (Argos 4 Common) can reduce maelstrom strength but it only does that for travel. That's why the roll is a perception roll; the Harbinger is finding the safest path, not forcibly quieting the storm. Maitre apres Dieu is the only one that can really mess your story and that's a level 5 initiate power, so you have lots of reason to disallow it on a starting character. Conversely, that power would make a lot of sense for your NPC.<br /> <br /> As far as Pathos is concerned, make sure all the characters have Passions that they can engage in as a part of this crew. Unless you plan on having shore leave time, they aren't going to have the chance to gather it from the Quick. Play up the intercharacter conflict that comes from enclosed spaces and tense environments, it's not just story fodder, it is their chance to feed. Also make sure they have Dark Passions that are applicable. While they might not want their Shadows to feed, you do. <br /> <br /> I'd add multiple incarnations of Troy to your list. Troy II, Troy VI, and Troy VII would be good candidates as those appear to have potentially violent ends. I'd also suggest having some locations that are just buildings rather than the entire city.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T06:18:10-07:00","id":1487876,"title":"","content":"I did some of my own rules in an adaptation I did for Gurps (half complete). You can find those here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forums.sjgames.com/showthread.php?t=180897&amp;page=7\" target=\"_blank\">http://forums.sjgames.com/showthread...=180897&amp;page=7</a><br /> <br /> For Argos, it just depends on the level they have on it actually. Just limit it and it's fine; adjust where necessary. If not enough, just place some special rules for it to where they are, but be sure to give something in it's place instead. So, if simply teleporting to the nearest necropolis is too much, let them do something like blinking in combat - adding their argos rating to Dexterity etc, something like that.<br /> <br /> For recovery, being away and isolated is quite enough to make it harder already, while still not impossible.<br /> <br /> <b>Interesting cities:</b><br /> <br /> - Tenochtitl\u00e1n - the former capital of the Aztecs (nowadays, Mexico City). In my opinion, this one would be even cooler than Atlantida - and possibly a massive spectral nightmarish town<br /> - Machu Pichu (Incan Empire)<br /> - Tikal (largest mayan city)<br /> <br /> So, those 3 were the main pre columbian american cities, respectfully for the aztecs, incans and mayans. Those are great places for said purpose, with pagan gods, high culture and a prevalence of human sacrifices. Possibly specter infested places of nightmares.<br /> <br /> Other than those:<br /> <br /> - Atlantis (classic)<br /> - Pompey - great place for the underworld, destroyed by a Vulcano<br /> - Troy - another mythic (and real!) place. Maybe you'll even find Achilles in it!<br /> - El Dourado - this one, like Atlantis, is fully mythical - but in the Tempest, all goes. You may find a bunch of spaniards conquistadors cutthroats and mercenaries in an obscessive quest to try to enter it.<br /> - Sparta - barely nothing is left of it irl. If you want realism thou, be warned that the spartans were a bunch of cowards and traitors, and their society were entirely based on slavery, and that spartans were only ever trained to SUPRESS THEIR SLAVES who far outnumbered them, not to fight in wars - which is why they were such cowards. But you can go along with the false narrative of the movies if you'd like.<br /> - Memphis - the most important capital of ancient Egypt. Again, awesome place. Maybe you'll find some mummies, or perhaps even Anubis!<br /> - Babylon - love ziggurats? Well, look no further than the old capital of the Babylonian Empire!<br /> - Tyre, Sidon, Byblos - the main Phoenician cities<br /> - Pasargadae, the first capital of the ancient Persian Empire.<br /> - Dvaraka, modern Dwarka: one of the 7 sacred cities of hinduims, and home of Krishna himself. The ancient city was destroyed, modern Dwarka was built in it's place (much like Troy was destroyed and rebuilt several times). Maybe you can find Krishna himself!<br /> - Camelot (another mythical)<br /> - Alexandria - this one would be in my top 3 choices, and the reason is almost self evident.<br /> - Shangri-la - another mythical one<br /> <br /> I would add the Terracota Army and the emperor's tomb, but those are already part of the Dark Kingdom of Jade so, that's out.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's an starting pick from the top of my head, but do a small search and you'll find countless more","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T09:07:37-07:00","id":1487889,"title":"","content":"For cities and places I would like to stick with historical ones. I like the idea of equating 'going deeper' into the Tempest with going back in time, and I also have a player with a PhD in history, so I feel obligated to at least put in some research and give him a few moments of recognizing the places OOC. The different layers of Troy are a great choice for that, but I might want a wider spread geographically and culturally. There's also an ancient Egypt buff among the players, so Alexandria, Memphis, or Bubastis are likely candidates. If I can pull it off I want the encounters in those places to have some allegorical relevance to the characters, so my picks will also be partially based on that. Having many options helps until I know what the characters are like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1487850-need-some-ideas-for-nautical-themed-tempest-adventure?p=1487875#post1487875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also suggest having some locations that are just buildings rather than the entire city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you have something specific in mind for this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1487850-need-some-ideas-for-nautical-themed-tempest-adventure?p=1487875#post1487875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going by the powers listed in Wr20, I don't think you have much to worry about until the Argos 5 Initiate power. Most of the powers are effectively personal. Stormreader (Argos 4 Common) can reduce maelstrom strength but it only does that for travel. That's why the roll is a perception roll; the Harbinger is finding the safest path, not forcibly quieting the storm. Maitre apres Dieu is the only one that can really mess your story and that's a level 5 initiate power, so you have lots of reason to disallow it on a starting character. Conversely, that power would make a lot of sense for your NPC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're right. I may have thought of some old or alternative Arts. And yeah, the Argos 5 Initiate power is like tailor-made for the NPC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1487850-need-some-ideas-for-nautical-themed-tempest-adventure?p=1487875#post1487875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as Pathos is concerned, make sure all the characters have Passions that they can engage in as a part of this crew. Unless you plan on having shore leave time, they aren't going to have the chance to gather it from the Quick. Play up the intercharacter conflict that comes from enclosed spaces and tense environments, it's not just story fodder, it is their chance to feed. Also make sure they have Dark Passions that are applicable. While they might not want their Shadows to feed, you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is extremely helpful, thank you. I don't plan on having shore leaves- I should probably have a proper chargen session with the group so I can guide them a bit with stat choices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1487850-need-some-ideas-for-nautical-themed-tempest-adventure?p=1487876#post1487876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did some of my own rules in an adaptation I did for Gurps (half complete). You can find those here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forums.sjgames.com/showthread.php?t=180897&amp;page=7\" target=\"_blank\">http://forums.sjgames.com/showthread...=180897&amp;page=7</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I will probably focus more on drama than tables, but this is nice!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T09:52:07-07:00","id":1487899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1487850-need-some-ideas-for-nautical-themed-tempest-adventure?p=1487889#post1487889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you have something specific in mind for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>The first temple of Jerusalem comes to mind. Well both do, but the first is older, less likely to be claimed by Stygian when it was destroyed, and was destroyed and rebuilt on several occasions so there are more moments to choose from. Also, given how central it was to the entire culture, its relic would be far more durable than the rest of the city.<br /> <br /> Most single buildings from that far back are going to be temples or religious sites, come to think of it. They were the more durable and had the most emotional investment, so they had stronger emotional investment from more people than anything else.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T20:22:33-07:00","id":1487969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1487850-need-some-ideas-for-nautical-themed-tempest-adventure?p=1487899#post1487899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The first temple of Jerusalem comes to mind. Well both do, but the first is older, less likely to be claimed by Stygian when it was destroyed, and was destroyed and rebuilt on several occasions so there are more moments to choose from. Also, given how central it was to the entire culture, its relic would be far more durable than the rest of the city.<br /> <br /> Most single buildings from that far back are going to be temples or religious sites, come to think of it. They were the more durable and had the most emotional investment, so they had stronger emotional investment from more people than anything else.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>All the 7 world wonders could appear in the Tempest, if they werent claimed by one of the Dark Kingdoms, except for the pyramids of Gyze which still exists. So, it's the Babylonian Hanging Gardens, the Colussus of Rhodes, the Pathenon. Terracota like I said is unfortunately out, due to it being the Jade Emperor's army, but many many more things go. For Egypt itself there would be a ton of stuff there - sadly thou, most of what was lost has also been lost to history, so we have no idea of what might have been. The Sphinx for example, I would say that it may be debatable if the original one couldnt be in the underworld, with vibrant colors, since what we have is just a carcass of what it truly was.<br /> <br /> Since the players would be in a submarine, Atlantis would be the first thing to pop into mind, however that's purely mythical. For a real place thou, the minoan civilization of Crete would be an awesome substitute - many historians even believe that the myth of Atlantis may have been an adaptation of the history of Crete. There's also the possibility that the minoan civilization of Crete was destroyed by a tsunami, so it would fit well with the theme of an underwater &quot;aquaman&quot; city. You could even introduce the fabled Labyrinth, and maybe even a plasmic (or a few) Minotaur! And maybe you could even find the mythical hero Teseu there! (or something that claims to be him).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T07:50:02-07:00","id":1488027,"title":"","content":"The Onyx tower is allegedly built on the relic stones of the Lighthouse of Alexandria, so that one is spoken for... maybe. The Lighthouse, Mausoleum, Temple of Artemis, and Statue of Zeus were all destroyed late enough that Stygia would be in place to scoop them up. That doesn't mean it did, just that there's a story there if it didn't.<br /> <br /> If the lighthouse is somewhere in the Tempest it would be a great safe haven. <br /> <br /> <br /> There's a theory that the story of Midas grew because the tin deposits in the region was contaminated with zinc, so the bronze made with it took on a brass sheen, which would have made it look more-gold like. I bring this up because if they explore the ruins of Phrygia they could find relics or substances that could be worked into soulsteel to give it special properties.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 07-26-2022, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T09:08:19-07:00","id":1488034,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of diversifying the deep Tempest encounters with fragments (single buildings or monuments) instead of only cities, it keeps full city encounters fresh. I also want to cross-check with the descriptions of the Dark Kingdoms again; I'm not opposed to using elements that pop up in other parts of the setting per-se, but it would be neat if I can make it consistent. Pretty sure at least parts of Tenochtitlan for example ended up in the Dark Kingdom of Obsidian.<br /> <br /> But making the encounters down there more varied is now definitely on the agenda. I want at least one giant Wyrd attack at some point.<br /> <br /> Another point that I ran into is that I want to keep the literal pressure of the deep. I think I will just treat the water as a solid object after a certain point, so players can still have short excursions outside the vessel but are on a time limit. Sunken cities can still exist in a bubble so they won't be affected- although exploring a drowned version of a famous site sounds cool, too.<br /> <br /> Also, slight change to the story setup: the part of his Psyche the Ferryman is hunting got attached to his Pasiphae when it separated. Not sure why I didn't see that sooner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1487850-need-some-ideas-for-nautical-themed-tempest-adventure?p=1488027#post1488027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a theory that the story of Midas grew because the tin deposits in the region was contaminated with zinc, so the bronze made with it took on a brass sheen, which would have made it look more-gold like. I bring this up because if they explore the ruins of Phrygia they could find relics or substances that could be worked into soulsteel to give it special properties.</div> </div> </div> </div>On that note, I'm leaning towards recommending my players an Alchemist over an Artificer if any of them wants to pick up the engineer role. Flux is just better suited for maintaining a relic vessel. Sea of Shadows also offers an alternate Art for Fatalism, so I consider tweaking it further for an Oracle navigator.<br /> <br /> I really appreciate the input so far, it's been very useful!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"h