path.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T12:06:55-07:00","id":1488272,"title":"","content":"For examples of cities sunk into the depths of the Tempest, I would only select cities that are truly and utterly destroyed. Not just cities that have ruins. Tenochtitlan still exists, it is just called Mexico City. Alexandria still exists. Rome still exists.<br /> <br /> Individual buildings that have been destroyed can still show up, but they usually appear in the Shadowlands first. And if important are sometimes disassembled and shipped off to Stygia to be reconstructed.<br /> <br /> So I'd be looking for cities that were destroyed - suddenly and totally would be best - and are now completely uninhabited. You want something truly catastrophic for it to slip into the Tempest instead of appearing in the Shadowlands that could be pillaged by wraiths. Cities that gradually went into decline and slowly abandoned probably aren't the best choices. Their sudden destruction would provide drama that creates a hook or story for the location. For our purposes, I think even possibly or likely fictional cities are OK provided there are real legends attesting to their existence. Here are some examples that come to my mind.<ul><li>Sodom &amp; Gomorrah (destroyed by God in the Old Testament)</li> <li>Irem/Ubar (mentioned in the Koran, supposedly destroyed by a sandstorm)</li> <li>Akrotiri (destroyed by the Thera volcanic explosion in the Bronze Age)</li> <li>Troy (as already mentioned by Ramnensis, but I'd go full Iliad/Trojan War here inspired more by legend than historical reality simply because that is cooler)</li> <li>Vilcabamba (the lost capital city of the Incas sacked by the Spaniards)</li> <li>Vineta (the probably fictitious &quot;Atlantis of the Baltic&quot; lost in the 12th century)</li> <li>Pompeii (already mentioned)</li> <li>Tanis (the Egyptian city where Indian Jones finds the lost Ark of the Covenant in Raiders of the Lost Ark. Its history there is fictional, not historical, but I'd use that because it is cooler.)</li> <li>Karakorum (the Mongol capital razed by Ming troops in 1388)</li> <li>Camelot (the castle/court/town of King Arthur)</li> <li>Port Royal (Jamaican pirate town destroyed by earthquake in 1692)</li> <li>Roanoke Colony (British colony lost to mystery, but in the World of Darkness the site of the destruction of the Croatan tribe of Garou against the Eater-of-Souls)</li> <li>Lyonesse (legendary island/city sunk overnight, from Arthurian legend)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T04:52:51-07:00","id":1488350,"title":"","content":"Ohh Port Royal is an awesome idea... A pirate city - and we all know, pirates are awesome.<br /> <br /> It could even have a few spectral vessels raiding all the unfortunate souls that end up there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T08:12:21-07:00","id":1488362,"title":"","content":"Port Royal is actually mentioned in <i>Blood-Dimmed Tides</i> (thanks again <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> ) as a Necropolis of note and gets a description. The book has a long section for WtO focused on Ghost Ships and piracy.<br /> <br /> Other useful tidbits I got out of it:<br /> - Water is solid for Wraiths by default. Who knew? Not me.<br /> - Some dedicated Merits/Flaws and alternate Arts<br /> - Interestingly, Monitors are used as navigators (triangulating with fetters). I still prefer Oracles for the role, fate-powered navigation is just too cool to dismiss<br /> - The shroud/tempest wall is paper-thin in deep Skinland oceans. So if I need a trip to the Skinlands, that's actually less of a problem than I thought.<br /> <br /> As for cities, I agree that (violently) destroyed ones are better for use. I don't want to exhaust the experience, so I will probably narrow the selection to three or four and pepper them with single buildings or small sites in between. It gets a bit philosophical which city counts as destroyed rather than abandoned and decayed, since many where rebuilt and lived on under different names. For example, would Byzantium count, or did it just become Istanbul? Sites like Pompeii and Herculaneum are definitively easier to categorize in this regard.<br /> <br /> I also remembered Doggerland, a previously inhabited land-bridge between the British Isles and the continent that sunk beneath the waves in just 300 years or so. I may keep that one for a WtA game though.<br /> <br /> I'm currently building the <i>Dolomedes,</i> the Type VII-C U-Boat that will be the relic vessel. It's a really fun part of the scenario prep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 07-29-2022, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T08:18:06-07:00","id":1488364,"title":"","content":"Byzantium probably wouldnt count, since there's a continuity. But singular buildings could be floating there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T12:26:41-07:00","id":1488379,"title":"","content":"I also recommend that you watch the movie What Dreams May Come from 1998. It is based on a book by Richard Matheson who extensively studied stories of the afterlife by people who came back from death. It has so many things that directly translate to Wraith. I have to imagine the book (since the movie postdates Wraith) was a major influence on the game's designers or it is an incredible coincidence. There is one section in particular relevant for this thread, and that is when Chris (Robin William's character) enlists the Tracker (Max von Sydow) to take him on a voyage to Hell to rescue his wife. It's the closest thing in cinema on wraiths travelling the Tempest.<br /> <br /> This link is a ten minute synopsis of the movie, and the relevant scene is discussed starting at the six minute mark.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=imjTftLUfwU\" data-code=\"imjTftLUfwU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/imjTftLUfwU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Even if all you do is fast forward to that scene in the movie, I think there will be a lot you can take from this for your chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T09:52:26-07:00","id":1488716,"title":"","content":"I can't say why, but in my mind's eye, the Tempest always had the almost impenetrable visual quality of TV static. The wailing souls are spot on though.<br /> As a tangent, Mirrormask has may not have the best story, but visually is pretty close to how I imagine the Shadowlands and Necropolises.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I think I found a good image for the Wyrd that's going to be a fight encounter with this <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Haeckel_Siphonophorae_37.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">siphonophore</a> drawing by Haeckel.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T10:18:23-07:00","id":1488722,"title":"","content":"That's common for the tempest. There are surprisingly few detailed descriptions of it so people tend to fill in. I tend to think of it as the inside of a roiling thunderstorm with a sickly pinkish- purplish shade. The color is a muted shade of the one for Dimension X in the 80's TMNT show. I have no idea why that has any influence on my view of the Tempest but it does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T11:18:18-07:00","id":1488728,"title":"","content":"Oh! Mine has the purple, too. Come to think of it, a lot of 80s/90s cartoon shows and comics used that color scheme for those banishment dimensions- probably also an influence on my imagination. Strangely, other umbral geography doesn't share it. I guess the Tempest is pretty much the Phantom Zone of the WoD.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-th